# AutoMyBiz List Puncher - Conductor Rules

Role: Senior Vanilla-JS Front-End Engineer & YAML Format Steward for "AutoMyBiz List Puncher".

This file is the source of truth for how this project must be maintained. Its goal is to prevent breaking
existing functionality while allowing new features - and to stop us re-learning expensive lessons twice.

---

## 1. Project Purpose & Philosophy

**What it is:** A single-page, dependency-free "punch list" engine that is embedded inside GoHighLevel
(GHL) as a Custom Menu Link (rendered in an iframe). Agencies hand a client a live onboarding/checklist
board and track progress against it.

**Who uses it:** Agency admins (editors) and clients (viewers), usually on desktop Chrome.

**Philosophy (non-negotiable):**
- **Zero dependencies.** Pure vanilla JS. No jQuery, no frameworks, no CDN scripts, no bundlers, no build step.
- **Two files ship.** `index.html` (markup + one big `<script>`) and `index.css` (master stylesheet).
- **YAML is the data format and the product.** The YAML is what users copy into ChatGPT/Claude/Gemini and
  paste back. It must stay human-readable, AI-friendly and perfectly round-trippable.
- **Live theme driven.** Colors, borders and card FX come from a Google Sheet via a Cloudflare Worker, never
  from hardcoded values in JS.
- **Resilient.** Auto-save, cache-busting, self-checks and graceful fallbacks are core to the UX.

---

## 2. Architecture Map

| Concern | Where it lives |
|---|---|
| Markup + all app logic | `index.html` (one `<script>` block at the bottom) |
| Master stylesheet | `index.css` (linked as `index.css?v=<APP_BUILD>`) |
| Live theme fetch | `fetchAndApplyLiveTheme()` -> `https://ghl-custom-workflow-settings.automybiz.workers.dev/?action=styles&gsheet_globals_id=...` |
| Theme cache (FOUC guard) | `localStorage['automybiz_punch_theme_css']` + `<style id="epwDynamicThemeStyles">` |
| GHL context | URL params: `location_id`, `token`, `user_email`, `user_name`, `user_role`, `owner_email`, `editors`, `viewers`, `mode`, `project`, `gsheet_globals_id`, `location_name` |
| Permissions | `evaluatePermissions()` -> editor / viewer / restricted (`list_puncher_editors`, `list_puncher_viewers` GHL custom values) |
| Task state | `TASKS_DATA` (flat array; `level: 0` = milestone/section, `level >= 1` = task/subtask) |
| Persistent UI state | `UI_STATE` (sections, branches, notesOpen, autoNumber, completedAtBottom, nestStyle, depthColorMode) |
| Render pipeline | `renderAll()` -> section decks -> `renderTaskNodeTree()` (recursive, builds `.branch-rail` wrappers) |
| YAML engine | `parseYamlToTasks()` (dispatch) -> `parseStrictPuncherYaml()` / `parseLegacyShorthandYaml()`, `formatTasksSliceAsYaml()` + `yamlQuote()` / `pushYamlTextValue()`, `clampYamlNestingSteps()`, `prettifyModalYaml()` |
| Media engine | `isYouTubeURL()`, `isImageURL()`, `parseYouTubeEmbed()`, `buildVideoEmbedHtml()`, `loadLazyVideo()`, `convertURLsToMedia()` |

**Storage keys** (all prefixed by `LOCATION_ID` so one GHL sub-account can hold unlimited lists):
- `list_puncher_<LOCATION_ID>_projects` - project directory
- `list_puncher_<LOCATION_ID>_active_proj_id` - active project
- `list_puncher_<LOCATION_ID>_proj_<projId>_yaml` - the list itself
- `list_puncher_<LOCATION_ID>_proj_<projId>_ui_state` - UI_STATE for that list
- `list_puncher_yaml` - legacy/cross-key safety net (always written too)

---

## 3. THE CANONICAL YAML FORMAT (highest-risk area - read twice)

This exact shape is what the app writes, what it must read back, and what the AI prompt tells models to emit:

```yaml
# ==========================================
# CLOUDFLARE INFRASTRUCTURE
# ==========================================
- section: "Cloudflare Infrastructure"
  description: "Master DNS and edge routing configuration."
  tasks:
    - task: "[ ] Task Title"
      notes: "Helpful instructions or links"
      tasks:
        - task: "[x] Subtask Title"
          notes: |
            https://youtu.be/eqQfmTJD1A
            https://www.example.com/diagram.png
```

**Why a milestone is a list item:** one list holds N milestones. Repeating a bare `section:` key at the
document root is a *duplicate key* error in every real YAML parser (a regex reader would never notice).

**Why the checkbox sits inside the value and children need a key:** `- task: "[ ] Title"` costs 2 lines per
task (no `checked:` key) and keeps the `[ ]` / `[x]` state visible and greppable. Nesting is the one place
the grammar forces a key - a block sequence may never sit inside a block mapping without one - so children
hang off `tasks:`, the same name a milestone uses for its task list. That holds the vocabulary to 5 names:
`section` / `description` / `tasks` / `task` / `notes`.

**Hard rules:**
1. **The output must be VALID STANDARD YAML.** The old shorthand `- [ ] Task Title` is NOT valid YAML
   (PyYAML/js-yaml reject it: `[ ]` is an empty flow sequence, and a scalar list item can never also
   carry mapping keys), so 1.14 replaced it and 1.15 condensed it. A task is a mapping `- task: "[ ] X"`;
   a milestone is a root list item (`- section:`), never a repeated root key.
2. **The checkbox is the value's prefix**: `- task: "[ ] Title"` / `- task: "[x] Title"`. The writer never
   emits a `checked:` key (it is still READ, so an AI that adds one is harmless).
3. **One nesting step = 2 spaces**: a task's own keys sit at `dash + 2`, its `tasks:` children at
   `dash + 4`. Never tabs in output.
4. **Children live under the parent's `tasks:` key.** A bare indented `- task:` is invalid YAML
   (`expected <block end>, but found '-'`) because a sequence can never sit inside a mapping without a key.
   Reusing `tasks:` keeps the vocabulary at 5 names: `section` / `description` / `tasks` / `task` / `notes`.
5. **`notes:` / `description:` block bodies sit 2 spaces deeper than their key.** The value is trimmed
   before it is written, so the first body line never starts with whitespace - that is what lets YAML
   auto-detect the body indentation (no explicit `|2` indicator needed).
   **NEVER align `notes:` with the task's dash.** Doing so puts the notes body at the same indent as child
   tasks, so on reload the parser swallows every following subtask into the notes block - the list appears to
   "never save". (This exact bug shipped once. Do not repeat it.)
6. **Every scalar is double-quoted** (`yamlQuote()`), escaping backslashes BEFORE quotes - a Windows path
   like `C:\Users\...` would otherwise be an illegal YAML escape sequence and break the whole document.
7. **Milestones are root list items**: `- section:` -> `description:` (optional) -> `tasks:` (or `tasks: []`
   when empty). Section titles are written WITHOUT leading numbers; the app numbers milestones dynamically.
8. **Unlimited depth** is allowed; the strict reader nests by dash indentation, so any step width (even the
   6/8/14-space mess a sloppy AI paste produces) still nests correctly.
9. **Legacy shorthand is still READ, never written.** `parseYamlToTasks()` dispatches: text matching
   `- task:` / `- title:` / `- section:` goes to `parseStrictPuncherYaml()` (which also accepts the 1.14
   `- title:` + `checked:` spelling and the `subtasks:` alias), anything else to `parseLegacyShorthandYaml()`
   (which still clamps depths). Old localStorage lists and old AI output keep loading; the next save rewrites
   them in the condensed shape, and `Prettify YAML` is the manual upgrader.
10. **Tabs used for indentation become 2 spaces** (`expandLeadingTabs()`); tabs inside a note stay (they are
    content, not layout).
11. **Media lives in notes**: bare YouTube URLs become lazy video facades; bare image URLs become `<img>`s.
12. **Round-trip is law.** Any serializer change must satisfy: `parse(format(x)) === x` and
    `format(parse(format(x))) === format(x)` (idempotent), AND `format(x)` must parse cleanly in a REAL YAML
    parser (PyYAML/js-yaml). `saveState()` re-parses what it wrote and flags the
    storage pill with "Save check failed" if the item count would change.

**Editor UX that must keep working:** the YAML modal (full / milestone / branch modes), `Prettify YAML`
(tabs -> 2 spaces, clamp, strip section numbers), and **TAB / SHIFT+TAB = indent / outdent 2 spaces**
(Notepad++ style, multi-line aware, caret preserved).

---

## 4. CSS, Theme & Nesting Rules

**Two independent toggles - never let one break the other:**
- **Nesting style** (`body.nest-style-rails` | `body.nest-style-cards`): rails ON draws the continuous
  left guide rails; rails OFF hides them (transparent border keeps the exact same 14px indent).
- **Depth colors** (`body.depth-colors-alt` | `body.depth-colors-solid`): ALT gives **one alternating color
  per nesting level** (level 1/3 = `--card-border-color-1`, level 2/4 = `--card-border-color-2`) for BOTH the
  rail and the row hook at that depth; SOLID uses one theme color everywhere.

**Cascade rules (learned the hard way):**
1. **State classes live on `<body>`.** Because of that, they must be written as ONE compound selector:
   `body.fx-state.card-border-animated .section-deck` matches; `body.fx-state .card-border-animated ...`
   **can never match** (the space demands a descendant carrying the class). Verify with a harness that models
   each selector part as a DISTINCT element in the ancestor chain - pooling ancestor classes hides this bug.
2. **Mode-scoped overrides win by specificity + source order**, and rail colors are scoped to
   `.nest-style-rails` so they can never resurrect hidden rails.
3. **Only add `:root` variables when asked**, and reuse existing tokens first (`--card-border-color-1/2`,
   `--accent-*`, `--text-*`). Match the stylesheet's existing convention: hex colors, `rgba()` for translucency.
4. **Never auto-disable or degrade the decorative card FX.** Do not add `prefers-reduced-motion` overrides,
   do not step/slow the beam, do not auto-pause it on blur/hover/tab-change. The owner explicitly wants the
   animation running at all times; a previous "FX throttle" did all of the above and was fully reverted.
5. **Live theme owns the animation knobs**: `--card-border-speed`, `CARD_BORDER_ANIMATE_ENABLE`,
   `CARD_BORDER_ANIMATE_SPEED`, `CARD_BORDER_ANIMATE_EFFECT` (adds `effect-<name>` to `<body>`). If the border
   ever stops moving, check those sheet tokens before touching CSS.
6. Keep the deck beam and the section-header beam smooth: `animation: ... linear infinite` (not stepped).

---

## 5. Media & Video Rules (click-only, always)

1. **The YouTube player is created ONLY when the user clicks.** Render a lazy facade (poster + play button)
   and hydrate it in `loadLazyVideo()`. A player created on page load sits idle and eventually shows a
   ~20s black screen on the first click. This was the single biggest video bug in this project.
2. **Never load media on hover.** Click-based only - hovering many rows must stay free of work.
3. **Embed URL contract:** `https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` plus `list=`, `start=` from the
   source URL, then `autoplay=1&rel=0&playsinline=1&enablejsapi=1` on hydration. Keep `youtube-nocookie.com`
   (the `youtube.com` embed path triggers an anti-ad-block black-screen timeout for users running ad blockers)
   and keep `web-share` in the iframe `allow` list.
4. **Media clicks must `stopPropagation()`** - the media lives inside the task-notes block, whose click handler
   opens the notes editor. Without it, clicking play turns the note into a textarea instead of playing.
5. **Poster** = `https://i.ytimg.com/vi/<id>/hqdefault.jpg`, hidden via `onerror` so the URL text remains a
   valid click target if the thumbnail fails.
6. Keep the `<link rel="preconnect">` hints for `youtube-nocookie.com` and `i.ytimg.com`.
7. Images stay as `<img loading="lazy">` with `onclick="event.stopPropagation(); window.open(...)"`.

---

## 6. Storage & Data Safety Rules

1. **Write the list to every relevant key** (project key + `list_puncher_yaml`) so a key mismatch or a missing
   URL param can never orphan the user's data; on load, fall back: project key -> legacy key -> blueprint.
2. **Never overwrite stored YAML with an empty list.** Guard writes so a transient empty `TASKS_DATA` cannot
   wipe real work.
3. **Verify every save**: `saveState()` round-trips what it wrote and returns a status the storage pill shows
   ("✓ Saved" vs "⚠ Save check failed"). Keep that honesty - the pill is the user's only signal that a refresh
   will be safe.
4. **Auto-save is debounced at 500ms** (`AUTOSAVE_DELAY_MS`) with a flush on `beforeunload`.
5. Per-project state (collapsed sections, open notes, toggles) lives in `_ui_state`, never in the YAML.

---

## 7. Build, Version & Cache Discipline

This is a static GitHub Pages site with a separated stylesheet, so **stale caches are a real failure mode**
(a new `index.html` can arrive next to an old `index.css`, silently disabling new CSS rules).

**Every deploy bumps all three, together:**
1. `const APP_BUILD = '<n>'` in `index.html`
2. `<link rel="stylesheet" href="index.css?v=<n>">`
3. `--lp-css-build: "<n>"` in `index.css` `:root`

`guardAgainstStaleStylesheet()` compares (2)+(3) against (1) and warns the user to hard-refresh
(Ctrl+Shift+R) when they disagree. Never remove that guard - it is the only thing that makes a
"it didn't work" report distinguishable from "you are running the old file".

**Verification after pushing:** wait ~1-2 minutes for the Pages build, then fetch
`https://automybiz.github.io/AutoMyBiz-List-Puncher/index.css?v=<n>` and confirm the version string.
Always tell the owner to hard-refresh and how to confirm the live build.

---

## 8. Testing & Validation Protocol (before every commit)

1. **Extract and run the real code, never a re-implementation.** Pull the actual functions out of
   `index.html` (brace-matched extraction) and exercise them in Node.
2. **Mandatory harnesses:**
   - **YAML round-trip**: `parse(format(x))` keeps every item/title/level/checked/notes, and
     `format(parse(format(x)))` is byte-identical. Include multi-line notes followed by subtasks.
   - **CSS cascade**: resolve the winning declaration for each toggle combination with a DOM model where
     each selector part must match a **distinct** ancestor element; include negative tests for selectors that
     must NOT match.
   - **Media engine**: facades render with no eager `<iframe>`, hydration keeps `start=`, adds autoplay, and
     the click handler stops propagation.
   - **Tab handler**: indent/outdent single line, multi-line, stray space and no-op cases.
3. `node --check` the extracted `<script>` block (syntax gate).
4. **Grep for dangling references** to anything renamed or deleted (expect 0 matches).
5. **Delete the temporary harnesses** afterwards and confirm `git status` shows only the intended files.
6. **Never claim "verified" for something simulated loosely.** State what was actually executed.

---

## 9. Git & Commit Rules

- **Conventional commits**, imperative mood: `fix:`, `feat:`, `revert:`, `chore:`.
- **One concern per commit**, and keep changes revert-friendly: isolated blocks, documented flags
  (e.g. `LAZY_VIDEO_FACADE = false`) and explicit `<<< REVERT ... >>>` markers where useful.
- **Always push** after committing (`git push origin main`) so the owner can test on the live Pages site,
  then report the commit hash and what to expect.
- Never force-push, never rewrite pushed history, never commit temp files or `.tmp_*` harnesses.
- Shell note for this machine: use `git --no-pager`, wrap `-m` messages in **single quotes** and avoid
  embedded double quotes (PowerShell splits them and git then treats the words as pathspecs).

---

## 10. Communication Rules (how to work with this owner)

1. **Say plainly when a theory was wrong.** When a fix is disproven, state it in one line and move on - no spin.
2. **Every change comes with a user-testable step** ("hard-refresh, click X, you should see Y").
3. **Flag backward-compatibility risk BEFORE shipping**, especially anything touching the YAML format,
   default toggle states or stored data.
4. **Ask before:** adding `:root` variables, changing default behavior, adding new UI controls, or altering
   the YAML format.
5. **Respect the owner's UI taste.** Toggles belong in the header button grid, matching `btn-action btn-toggle`
   styling and the `label: STATE` convention; keep the dark-teal/magenta aesthetic and the dense-but-readable
   two-tier task rows.
6. **Do not ask permission for the obvious small stuff** - read the files, diagnose, fix, verify, then report.

---

## 11. Known Traps (post-mortems - do not repeat)

| Trap | Symptom | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| `body.state .class-on-body ...` selector | New CSS rule never applies ("nothing changed") | Compound the body classes: `body.state.class-on-body` |
| `notes:` aligned with the task dash | Saved list loses subtasks on refresh ("YAML never saves") | Notes key at +2, body at +4 |
| Shorthand `- [ ] Title` written as output | Gemini/PyYAML/js-yaml report the whole document as invalid YAML | Emit `- task: "[ ] Title"` (mapping form); shorthand is read-only legacy |
| Indented `- task:` with no children key above it | `expected <block end>, but found '-'` - the whole file is invalid | Children hang off `tasks:`; a sequence can never sit inside a mapping without a key |
| Quoting a bare dash line (`- "[ ] Title"` + `notes:`) | Still invalid - a scalar item cannot also carry mapping keys | The quotes must sit on a `task:` value |
| Player iframe created on page load | ~20s black screen on first play click | Click-only lazy facade |
| `youtube.com/embed` + ad blocker | Black screen / playback timeout | Use `youtube-nocookie.com` + autoplay params |
| Media click not stopped | Clicking play opens the note editor instead | `event.stopPropagation()` on media |
| Stepped / paused / reduced-motion FX | Border frozen ("colored but not moving") | Never throttle the decorative FX |
| Stale `index.css` after deploy | New CSS rules silently ignored | `?v=` cache-bust + `--lp-css-build` guard |
| Loosely simulated CSS harness | Shipped a selector that could never match | Model distinct ancestors + negative tests |

---

## 12. Do-Not-Break Checklist (run before shipping)

- [ ] YAML round-trips: save -> reload keeps every task, subtask, checkbox and multi-line note.
- [ ] Rails ON/OFF and Colors ALT/SOLID still produce four distinct, correct looks.
- [ ] Card FX animates smoothly and is never auto-paused, stepped or motion-disabled.
- [ ] Videos: no player until clicked; one click plays; media clicks never open the note editor.
- [ ] Images still render inline and open in a new tab.
- [ ] Drag/drop reorder + indent, auto-numbering, collapse-all, completed-at-bottom still work.
- [ ] Editor/viewer/restricted permission modes still gate editing.
- [ ] Live theme still applies from the sheet (colors, speed, effect class).
- [ ] `APP_BUILD`, `index.css?v=` and `--lp-css-build` all match the new version.
- [ ] Only the intended files are modified; no temp harnesses committed.

---

## 13. Breakthrough Protocol

Whenever a hard-won solution, discovery or convention is found during a task, **ask the owner whether it
should be immortalized in this file** (and add it if so). This file is the project's memory - keep it current,
and read it before making changes.

